[TYPE] Short description (50 chars max)

# Body: explain what and why, not how
# Wrap at 72 characters.



# Refs: link to issues, requirements, or risk controls
Refs: #

# ---
# TYPE must be one of:
#   REQ   - Implements a requirement (link to requirement/feature issue)
#   FIX   - Fixes a defect (link to bug issue)
#   TEST  - Adds or updates tests (link to related issue)
#   REFACTOR - No functional change (link to parent issue if applicable)
#   SOUP  - Dependency added/updated/removed
#   DOCS  - Documentation only
#   BUILD - Build system or CI changes
#   RELEASE - Version bump and release preparation
#
# Rules:
#   - Subject line: imperative mood ("Add feature" not "Added feature")
#   - Refs: at least one issue number for commits to main
#   - For feature branches: Refs optional on individual commits
#     (traceability enforced at PR merge via squash)
#
# IEC 62304 §8.2.4: Every change to main must be traceable to a
# requirement, problem report, or change request.
